# Target C: exact exclusion of two-singleton support 8

Date: 2026-09-29

Support 8 in the committed thirteen-support narrowing is

`[0123]^3 [0124] [0134] [0145] [0234] [0245] [1234]`.

This note records a complete orientation-level exclusion for that support in the
nine-no-root `k=4, D=-1, d_root=0, p=2` two-selected-singleton profile.

Companion verifier:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_nine_noroot_k4_dminus1_d0p2_two_singleton_support8_eight_empty_obstruction_2026_09_29.py`

## Structural lower bound on empty blocks

For every orientation of this support, the touched block family `T` has

`|T| = 15`, `rank H(T) = 9`.

Let `C` be the touched actual-complete blocks, `S` the touched selected-singleton
blocks, and `E` the touched actual-empty blocks. Because `d_root=0`, the rows
`H(C)` are independent, so `|C|=rank H(C)`. The established four-direction
capacity condition gives

`rank H(T) - rank H(C) >= 4`.

Hence `|C| <= 5`. Since at most two selected singleton blocks lie in `T`,

`|E| = 15 - |C| - |S| >= 15 - 5 - 2 = 8`.

Thus every realizable state contains at least eight touched actual-empty blocks.

## Exact eight-empty obstruction

There are six multiplicity-one supports after `[0123]^3`, so there are exactly
`3^6 = 729` raw orientation assignments. For each orientation, the verifier
examines all `C(15,8)=6435` eight-block subsets, for

`729 * 6435 = 4,691,115`

cases.

For an eight-block set `F`, let `U(F)` be the sum of the exact local
empty-block constraint spaces. If `F` were a set of actual-empty blocks, then
`U(F)` would be contained in the actual aggregate constraint space `W`, which
has dimension four.

The exact census is:

- `4,691,007` subsets have rank at least five already modulo 2;
- `108` subsets have rank four modulo 2;
- all `108` exceptional subsets have exact rational rank four;
- all `108` exact rank-four spaces fail the committed necessary generalized-weight
  filter `parity_profile_ok`.

Reduction modulo 2 cannot increase rank, so the first class cannot lie in a
four-dimensional rational space. In the second class, an actual eight-empty
set would have `U(F)=W`; but every such `U(F)` fails a necessary condition
for the actual `W`. Therefore no orientation is realizable.

The persisted verifier blob is
`b637000d1a23df649eece5428bc9bbf8d3ee033e`. That exact verifier source was
executed locally. Its imported current-main helper is
`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_nine_noroot_k4_dminus1_d0p2_selected_pair_orientation_2026_09_28.py`,
blob `867e8e583f6073c92b1f7afbf2aaf536e2567fa9`. The local execution used a
transcription of the relevant audited helper routines; as a cross-check, that
transcription exactly reproduced the committed support-5 census before the new
support-8 run.

## Consequence

Support 8 is excluded. On authoritative main before this contribution, supports
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 12 were already closed. Separate pushed branches contain
support-6 and support-7 exclusions but are not yet on main.

This closes support 8 only. It does not close the full two-singleton profile,
the full `D=-1,p=2` branch, or Erdos Problem #99.
